  "question": "1) Background / Context  \nThe project involves developing a database system to store and analyze data related to global national statistics and relationships between countries. This system is part of a larger effort to enhance data-driven decision-making and policy analysis.\n\n2) Objectives  \nThe primary objective is to create a relational database that can manage and query data about countries, their bilateral relations, and various socio-economic and political statistics. The system aims to facilitate comprehensive analysis and reporting on international indicators.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users  \n- Stakeholders:  \n  - International Policy Analysts  \n  - Researchers in Political Science and Economics  \n  - Government Agencies  \n  - Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs)  \n\n- Users:  \n  - Data Scientists  \n  - Policy Makers  \n  - Academic Researchers\n\n4) Functional Descriptions  \n- Database Management:  \n  The system will manage records for countries, including their ID and name.\n  \n- Relation Tracking:  \n  Facilitate storage and retrieval of relationships between countries with associated values like economic, political, and military ties.\n\n- Statistical Analysis:  \n  Maintain a wide range of statistics per country, such as population, economic indicators (e.g., GNP, exports/imports), social indicators (e.g., literacy, unemployment), and political metrics.\n\n- Reporting and Querying:  \n  Enable users to perform complex queries to generate customized reports analyzing international trends and relationships.\n\n- Data Integrity:  \n  Ensure data consistency and integrity through foreign key relationships and constraints.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions  \n- Scalability:  \n  The system should efficiently handle a growing amount of data as more countries and statistics are included.\n\n- Performance:  \n  Queries should return results within an acceptable timeframe to ensure efficient data analysis.\n\n- Security:  \n  Protect sensitive statistical data from unauthorized access and ensure compliance with data protection regulations.\n\n- Reliability:  \n  The system should provide reliable access to data without significant downtime.\n\n- Maintenance:  \n  The database system should support easy maintenance and upgrades without disrupting analytical processes.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0118\n\nCREATE TABLE `country` (\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`country_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `country_relation` (\n  `relation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country_id_1` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `country_id_2` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `economic_tie` decimal(15,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `political_tie` decimal(15,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `military_tie` decimal(15,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`relation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `country_relation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id_1`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `country_relation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id_2`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `country_statistics` (\n  `stat_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `country_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `population` bigint(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gnp` decimal(20,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `exports` decimal(20,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `imports` decimal(20,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `literacy_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unemployment_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gdp_per_capita` decimal(15,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inflation_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `government_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `political_stability_index` decimal(10,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`stat_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `country_statistics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`country_id`) REFERENCES `country` (`country_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
